  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We can calculate the surface area of a sphere using the formula\n\n$$\nS=4\\pi {r}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the sphere.\n\nSubstituting $r=\\frac{11}{2}\\,\\text{cm}$ into the formula, we obtain\n\n$$\nS=4\\pi {(\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}=121\\pi \\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
